        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7ec536ff-6c9c-5bbf-8945-6ba103bc747a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles\n- Places: The Forum, Los Angeles, Inglewood, California, United States\n- People: Margaret Court, Charles Luckman, Carl Johnson, Svend Nielsen\n- Concepts: 1973 Virginia Slims World Championship Series, indoor carpet courts, women's tennis tournament\n\nFacts:\n- The 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles was a women's tennis tournament played on indoor carpet courts at The Forum in Los Angeles, California, United States.\n- The 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles was part of the 1973 Virginia Slims World Championship Series.\n- In the final of the 1973 British Motor Cars of Los Angeles, 2,693 spectators watched first-seeded Margaret Court win the singles title and earn $6,000 in first-prize money.\n- The Forum is a multi-purpose indoor arena in Inglewood, California, adjacent to Los Angeles.\n- Charles Luckman designed The Forum, and engineers Carl Johnson and Svend Nielsen engineered the structure so that it had no major support pillars.",
